          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iObs4r6Eyy5pR0E7k"><h2>This Used To Be Me.</h2></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text inUVvkAQpL6UxCClF"><p>For years my weight was something I was always thinking about. I&apos;d lose weight, gain some back, try another approach and repeat the cycle.</p></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text imwuBRG0Gf5S6YtHi"><p>Eventually I lost over 100 pounds.</p></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ict21Z7wd2avE2n7E"><p>But the biggest breakthrough wasn&apos;t just losing it.</p></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iMMlQwqFMDV0LQ4m1"><p>It was finally reaching a point where staying slim stopped feeling like something I had to fight for every day.</p></div></div
