          ><div class="iHOirfbWqEoHv7QhD" data-instant-type="container"
            ><div class="ifhTtnULUWF33K8m2" data-instant-type="container"
              ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text irSYCdTLoD1FTDIzU"><p>02</p></div
              ><div class="iKdDtQzBJbJaNUcdy" data-instant-type="container"></div></div
            ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text ijmpB7lI0yfYKXPe2"><h3>Bitter Melon</h3></div
            ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text idcwAvsxoFV3ImQhQ"><p>Probably the last thing you&apos;d expect to taste like nothing.</p></div
            ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i6DhieOYzQfNGM5b8"
              ><p>Bitter melon has been used throughout Asian wellness traditions and studied for its potential role in supporting healthy blood-sugar and metabolic function. And its name is accurate: <strong>It is extremely bitter.</strong> That made it one of the biggest formulation challenges. We kept the extract in the formula while designing Special Water so your water can still taste remarkably normal.</p></div
